  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "Chandra pays an on-line service provider a fixed monthly fee plus an hourly charge for connect time. Her December bill was \\(\\$12.48,\\) but in January her bill was \\(\\$17.54\\) because she used twice as much connect time as in December. What is the fixed monthly fee?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$2.53\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$5.06\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$6.24\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$7.42\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$8.77\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "January had twice December's connect time, so its connect-time charge was twice December's charge. The fixed fee was the same in both months. Consequently, the increase in the bill equals one December-sized connect-time charge:\n\\[\n17.54-12.48=5.06\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nDecember's bill consisted of that usage charge plus the fixed fee. Subtracting the usage charge gives\n\\[\n12.48-5.06=7.42\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nThe fixed monthly fee is \\(\\boxed{\\$7.42}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
